        "original_id": "4fab2e9e-6b3e-5b90-95b8-42e16e7a2b0c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Civil Defence Forces, Revolutionary United Front, National Patriotic Front of Liberia\n- People: Foday Sankoh, Charles Taylor, Joseph Momoh\n- Events: Sierra Leone Civil War\n- Groups: Kamajors, Mende ethnic group\n\nFacts:\n- The Sierra Leone Civil War began on 23 March 1991 when the Revolutionary United Front, supported by special forces from Charles Taylor’s National Patriotic Front of Liberia, intervened in Sierra Leone to try to overthrow the government of Joseph Momoh.\n- The Sierra Leone Civil War lasted from 1991 to 2002, continued for 11 years, engulfed Sierra Leone, and caused more than 50,000 deaths.\n- The Civil Defence Forces was a paramilitary organization that fought in the Sierra Leone Civil War.\n- Much of the Civil Defence Forces was composed of the Kamajors, a group that is part of the larger Mende ethnic group.\n- Foday Saybana Sankoh, born on 17 October 1937 and died on 29 July 2003, founded and led the Revolutionary United Front during the Sierra Leone Civil War.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
